[23.281174, "o", "||PASSAGE_0000||\r\nWARNING: SIGNIFICANT DRUG INTERACTIONS WITH PAXLOVID\r\n- PAXLOVID includes ritonavir, a strong CYP3A inhibitor, which may lead to greater exposure of certain concomitant medications, resulting in potentially severe, life-threatening, or fatal events\r\n- Prior to prescribing PAXLOVID: 1) Review all medications taken by the patient to assess potential drug-drug interactions with a strong CYP3A inhibitor like PAXLOVID and 2) Determine if concomitant medications require a dose adjustment, interruption, and/or additional monitoring\r\n- Consider the benefit of PAXLOVID treatment in reducing hospitalization and death, and whether the risk of potential drug-drug interactions for an individual patient can be appropriately managed\r\n\r\n||PASSAGE_0001||\r\n1 INDICATIONS AND USAGE\r\nPAXLOVID is indicated for the treatment of mild-to-moderate coronavirus disease 2019 (COVID-19) in adults who are at high risk for progression to severe COVID-19, including hospitalization or death.\r\n\r\n||PASSAGE_0002||\r\nLimitations of Use\r\nPAXLOVID is not approved for use as pre-exposure or post-exposure prophylaxis for prevention of COVID-19 .\r\n\r\n||PASSAGE_0003||\r\n2.1\tImportant Dosage and Administration Information\r\nPAXLOVID is nirmatrelvir tablets co-packaged with ritonavir tablets. There are three different dose packs available:\r\n- PAXLOVID (nirmatrelvir; ritonavir) co-packaged for oral use 300 mg;100 mg\r\n- PAXLOVID (nirmatrelvir; ritonavir) co-packaged for oral use 150 mg;100 mg for patients with moderate renal impairment\r\n- PAXLOVID (nirmatrelvir; ritonavir) co-packaged for oral use 300 mg;100 mg (Day 1) and 150 mg;100 mg (Days 2-5) for patients with severe renal impairment\r\nNirmatrelvir must be co-administered with ritonavir. Failure to correctly co-administer nirmatrelvir with ritonavir may result in plasma levels of nirmatrelvir that are insufficient to achieve the desired therapeutic effect.\r\nPrescriptions should specify the numeric dose of each active ingredient within PAXLOVID . Completion of the fu\r\n"]
[23.283562, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@4b1b7b4fd079:/workspace# "]
[27.759377, "i", "python3 -c '\nimport json, re\nwith open(\"/workspace/data/public/labels.jsonl\") as f:\n    for line in f:\n        data = json.loads(line)\n        raw = data[\"label_raw\"]\n        passages = re.split(r\"\\|\\|(PASSAGE_\\d+)\\|\\|\", raw)\n        # passages[0] should be empty or whitespace\n        # passages[1] is PASSAGE_0000, passages[2] is the text, etc.\n        header = passages[0]\n        parsed_passages = {}\n        for i in range(1, len(passages), 2):\n            pid = passages[i]\n            text = passages[i+1].strip()\n            parsed_passages[pid] = text\n        print(data[\"drug_name\"], \"chunks length:\", len(data[\"chunks\"]), \"parsed passages length:\", len(parsed_passages))\n        # Check if they match\n        match = True\n        for i, chunk in enumerate(data[\"chunks\"]):\n            pid = f\"PASSAGE_{i:04d}\"\n            if pid not in parsed_passages:\n                match = False\n                print(f\"  Missing {pid} in parsed passages!\")\n                break\n            if chunk.strip() != parsed_passages[pid]:\n                match = False\n                print(f\"  Mismatch at {pid}!\")\n                print(\"Chunk:\", repr(chunk.strip()[:100]))\n                print(\"Parsed:\", repr(parsed_passages[pid][:100]))\n                break\n        if match:\n            print(f\"  All {len(data[\"chunks\"])} chunks match PASSAGE_0000 to PASSAGE_{len(data[\"chunks\"])-1:04d} exactly!\")\n'\n"]
