[112.416724, "o", "PASSAGE_0023: ↑ tamsulosin\r\nAvoid concomitant use with PAXLOVID....\r\nPASSAGE_0029: ↑ anticancer drugs\r\nAvoid co-administration of encorafenib or ivosidenib due to potential risk of serious adverse events such as QT interval prolongation. Avoid use of neratinib, venetoclax or ibrutini...\r\nPASSAGE_0031: ↑ rivaroxaban\r\nIncreased bleeding risk with rivaroxaban. Avoid concomitant use.\r\ndabigatranSee Pharmacokinetics, Clinical Drug Interaction Studies (12.3)....\r\nPASSAGE_0032: ↑ dabigatran\r\nIncreased bleeding risk with dabigatran. Depending on dabigatran indication and renal function, reduce dose of dabigatran or avoid concomitant use. Refer to the dabigatran product label f...\r\n"]
[112.416906, "o", "PASSAGE_0038: ↓ voriconazole\r\nAvoid concomitant use of voriconazole....\r\nPASSAGE_0056: aliskiren,ticagrelor,vorapaxar\r\n                                       clopidogrel\r\n↑ aliskiren↑ ticagrelor↑ vorapaxar\r\n↓ clopidogrel active metabolite\r\nAvoid concomitant use with PAXLOVID....\r\nPASSAGE_0065: glecaprevir/pibrentasvir\r\nAvoid concomitant use of glecaprevir/pibrentasvir with PAXLOVID....\r\nPASSAGE_0075: ↑ everolimus↑ sirolimus\r\nAvoid concomitant use of everolimus and sirolimus and PAXLOVID.\r\nRefer to the individual immunosuppressant product label and latest guidelines for further information....\r\nPASSAGE_0078: ↑ salmeterol\r\nAvoid concomitant use with PAXLOVID. The combination may result in increased risk of cardiovascular adverse events associated with salmeterol, including QT prolongation, palpitations, and...\r\nPASSAGE_0082: ↑ rimegepant\r\nAvoid concomitant use with PAXLOVID....\r\nPASSAGE_0087: ↑ suvorexant\r\nAvoid concomitant use of suvorexant with PAXLOVID....\r\nPASSAGE_0091: ↑ tadalafil\r\nAvoid concomitant use of tadalafil with PAXLOVID for pulmonary hypertension....\r\n"]
